<%/* The brand mark, as one partial.

     The header and the footer each drew their own inline SVG: a hexagon
     outline with a violet-to-cyan gradient and a dot in the middle. That
     mark was replaced everywhere else — favicon, apple-touch icon, the
     512px PWA icon, the Open Graph share card and the order push
     notification all render the three-card Z from brand/mark.js — but the
     two places a visitor actually looks kept the old one. So the icon in
     the browser tab and the logo on the page were different marks.

     Brand inconsistency is not only a design complaint here. A Merchant
     Center reviewer comparing the tab icon, the page logo and the share
     preview is checking whether this is one coherent business, and three
     different marks is a signal in the wrong direction.

     Geometry is copied from brand/mark.js rather than imported because
     `require` is not available in EJS template scope. The viewBox and the
     three shapes must stay identical to that file; it is the source of
     truth and everything generated comes from it.

     Locals: `size` (px, default 28), `id` (unique when more than one
     instance appears on a page). */%>
<%
  var _size = typeof size !== 'undefined' ? size : 28;
%>
<svg width="<%= _size %>" height="<%= _size %>" viewBox="0 0 512 512" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <rect x="104" y="104" width="304" height="74" rx="10" fill="currentColor"/>
  <polygon points="284,192 408,192 228,320 104,320" fill="currentColor"/>
  <rect x="104" y="334" width="304" height="74" rx="10" fill="currentColor"/>
</svg>
